{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_c46i2bajdn6mwqi7jipruzkfgt5m4j3pttep7qrong54r4n2wvxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wait, I see an issue. In `stbds_hmput_key`, when we go to the found_empty_slot section, the C code does:\n\n```c\nptrdiff_t i = (ptrdiff_t) stbds_arrlen(a);\nif ((size_t) i+1 > stbds_arrcap(a))\n  *(void **) &a = stbds_arrgrowf(a, elemsize, 1, 0);\nraw_a = STBDS_ARR_TO_HASH(a,elemsize);\n\nSTBDS_ASSERT((size_t) i+1 <= stbds_arrcap(a));\nstbds_header(a)->length = i+1;\n```\n\nThe trick here is that `stbds_arrgrowf` is called with the array `a`, NOT the addlen=1 increasing length, so we need length-tracking to be the full new length, not just incremented. Looking at C:\n- `i = arrlen(a)` — current length (note: this is the underlying length, not including the +1 for hash maps)\n- We grow if i+1 > cap, then assign length = i+1\n\nBut what about `bucket->index[pos & MASK] = i-1`? That assigns the user-facing index, which is `stbds_arrlen(a)-1` since the user's array is offset by 1 element.\n\nHmm, but this looks correct... Let me check the actual segfault more carefully. The bug might be in how `stbds_arrgrowf` behaves when grown. Let me reread:\n\nIn `stbds_arrgrowf`, when `a` is non-null and we realloc:\n```\nb = STBDS_REALLOC(NULL, (a) ? stbds_header(a) : 0, elemsize * min_cap + sizeof(stbds_array_header));\n```\n\nThat uses `realloc(NULL, prev, size)` — wait, no, `STBDS_REALLOC(c,p,s) realloc(p,s)` so that's `realloc(prev_header, size)`. So when `a != null`, the realloc preserves data. Good.\n\nBut looking at my Rust translation: when `a == null`, I call `realloc(NULL, total_size)` which is just malloc — correct. When `a != null`, I pass `header(a)` as the prev pointer — correct.\n\nOK, let me check what the bug might be. The issue might be that within `hmput_key`, when the table grows we update `table` — but the location we point at is also modified. Let me run the C library only to make sure it works:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1815,"cache_read_input_tokens":95307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1815,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e04de84a-34d9-44b7-84d5-d2c3ada16f87","uuid":"b9185077-b5fb-47f4-a43e-8b26cf7f68fd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_c46i2bajdn6mwqi7jipruzkfgt5m4j3pttep7qrong54r4n2wvxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_0174YURqo6AhAJ4c94neNtJN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/harvest-translate-rKn6nG/translated_rust/tests/single_lib.rs","content":"//! Test loading just one library to isolate bugs.\nuse libloading::{Library, Symbol};\nuse std::ffi::c_void;\nuse std::os::raw::c_int;\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug)]\nstruct StbdsArrayHeader {\n    length: usize,\n    capacity: usize,\n    hash_table: *mut c_void,\n    temp: isize,\n}\n\nunsafe fn hash_header_of(t: *mut c_void, elemsize: usize) -> *mut StbdsArrayHeader {\n    let arr = (t as *mut u8).sub(elemsize) as *mut c_void;\n    (arr as *mut StbdsArrayHeader).sub(1)\n}\n\ntype FnHmputKey = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void, usize, *mut c_void, usize, c_int) -> *mut c_void;\ntype FnHmdelKey =\n    unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void, usize, *mut c_void, usize, usize, c_int) -> *mut c_void;\ntype FnRandSeed = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(usize);\n\nfn run_test(lib_path: PathBuf, name: &str) -> usize {\n    unsafe {\n        let lib = Library::new(&lib_path).unwrap();\n        let put: Symbol<FnHmputKey> = lib.get(b\"stbds_hmput_key\").unwrap();\n        let del: Symbol<FnHmdelKey> = lib.get(b\"stbds_hmdel_key\").unwrap();\n        let seed: Symbol<FnRandSeed> = lib.get(b\"stbds_rand_seed\").unwrap();\n        seed(0x31415926);\n\n        #[repr(C)]\n        struct Entry {\n            key: c_int,\n            value: c_int,\n        }\n        let elemsize = std::mem::size_of::<Entry>();\n        let keysize = std::mem::size_of::<c_int>();\n\n        let mut map: *mut c_void = std::ptr::null_mut();\n        for k in 0..32 {\n            let mut key_local = k as c_int;\n            map = put(map, elemsize, &mut key_local as *mut c_int as *mut c_void, keysize, 0);\n            let temp = (*hash_header_of(map, elemsize)).temp;\n            let entry = (map as *mut Entry).offset(temp as isize);\n            (*entry).key = k as c_int;\n            (*entry).value = (k * 10) as c_int;\n            println!(\"{} put({})={}\", name, k, temp);\n        }\n        for k in [3, 7, 10, 25, 0, 31] {\n            let mut key_local = k as c_int;\n            map = del(\n                map,\n                elemsize,\n                &mut key_local as *mut c_int as *mut c_void,\n                keysize,\n                0,\n                0,\n            );\n            let temp = (*hash_header_of(map, elemsize)).temp;\n            println!(\"{} del({})={}\", name, k, temp);\n        }\n        (*hash_header_of(map, elemsize)).length\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn c_only_hmdel() {\n    let p = PathBuf::from(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"))\n        .join(\"c_src/build/libtranslated_rust.so\");\n    let len = run_test(p, \"C\");\n    println!(\"final length = {}\", len);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn rust_only_hmdel() {\n    let p = PathBuf::from(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"))\n        .join(\"target/release/libtranslated_rust.so\");\n    let len = run_test(p, \"RUST\");\n    println!(\"final length = {}\", len);\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1815,"cache_read_input_tokens":95307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1815,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e04de84a-34d9-44b7-84d5-d2c3ada16f87","uuid":"01ec0fd9-6ea3-43d4-baea-6f2d3b6b74af"}
